.TH TEA 1 "@DATE@" "tea @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tea \- tiny econometric assistant: a Stata-compatible data tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tea
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIfile.do\fR]
.br
.B tea-decaf
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIfile.do\fR]
.br
.B tea-qt
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tea
is a small, self-contained C program for the data work economists use
Stata for: import, clean, merge, reshape, define variables, estimate,
and graph.  It runs a subset of Stata's language with faithful
semantics: a do-file that runs in tea is intended to produce the same
output, to the printed digit, in Stata.
.PP
With no arguments, tea starts an interactive REPL (GNU readline line
editing, persistent history, tab completion of commands and variable
names).  With a \fIfile.do\fR argument it runs the do-file in batch and
exits with its status.  A file argument of
.B \-
reads the script from standard input.
.PP
tea is strict-Stata by default: constructs that exist only in tea are
rejected unless
.B \-\-tea\-extensions
is given, which guarantees that every accepted do-file also runs
unchanged in Stata.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-strict\-stata
Reject tea-only language extensions (the default).
.TP
.B \-\-tea\-extensions
Allow tea-only extensions.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Suppress the startup banner.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
End of options; treat the next argument as a filename.
.SH INTERACTIVE USE
Type
.B help
for the themed command index,
.B help \fICMD\fR
for one command's syntax, and
.B sysuse dir
to list the practice datasets compiled into the binary.  Long output
pages when
.B set more on
is active (space advances a page, Enter one line,
.B q
abandons the rest of the command's output; the session log always
receives everything).  Ctrl\-D exits.
.SH COMPANION PROGRAMS
.TP
.B tea-decaf
The data-management tier: the same binary minus the entire estimation
layer (no regress, no time-series or panel estimators, no LAPACK in
the link).  Data prepared in decaf saves to Stata-compatible
.I .dta
for estimation in any full package.  Built with
.BR "make decaf" .
.TP
.B tea-qt
The native Qt desktop shell: a terminal-style console, a
virtual-scrolling data browser over the live dataset, a do-file
editor with run-selection, an SVG plots pane, and a Break button.
Built with
.BR "make gui" .
.PP
A browser build (WebAssembly, runs entirely client-side) is published
at
.IR https://micomrkaic.github.io/tea/ ,
with the decaf tier at
.IR https://micomrkaic.github.io/tea/decaf/ .
.SH FILES
tea is a self-contained binary: bundled datasets and help text are
compiled in, and it runs correctly from any working directory.  The
files it touches are its outputs:
.TP
.I ~/.tea_history
Interactive command history (capped at 2000 lines).
.TP
.I ./tea_graph.svg
Graph commands write their output here, in the current directory.
.TP
.I log files
Created where
.B log using
points.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; non-zero when a batch do-file aborts on an error (the
Stata return code is reported in the output).
.SH EXAMPLES
Run a do-file in batch:
.PP
.nf
    tea analysis.do
.fi
.PP
Clean data interactively, then hand it to Stata:
.PP
.nf
    tea
    . sysuse weo
    . keep if iso == "USA"
    . save usa.dta
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
The full manual:
.I tea-manual.pdf
(installed under \fIshare/doc/tea\fR, also at the repository root).
The compatibility contract:
.IR COMPATIBILITY.md .
The tiers:
.IR DECAF.md ,
.IR GUI.md .
Repository:
.IR https://github.com/micomrkaic/tea .
.SH BUGS
Known divergences from Stata are catalogued in
.I KNOWN_BUGS.md
(and its PDF) with root causes and status.  Report new ones at the
repository's issue tracker.
